{{/* The wizard's exit control, in its own fragment because it has to be
     re-patched alongside a card whose state changed. It was previously
     rendered once with the page while only the card was patched, so after the
     last enrolment finished it still carried the label ("Skip remaining") and
     the disabled attribute it was born with — a completed wizard whose only
     control was dead. Nothing here is disabled any more: leaving mid-run is
     harmless (the enrolment runs server-side and can be watched from
     /ui/enrolments/), and a disabled control is exactly what went stale.

     The two states are different in kind, so they are different elements.
     With everything addressed there is nothing to decide and the control is a
     plain link to the root, which re-derives on the server where the user
     belongs. With enrolments still outstanding, leaving *means* something —
     abandon the rest — so it stays a POST: a link to "/" would be answered by
     handleRoot with a redirect straight back to this page, which is precisely
     the case this control exists for. */}}
{{define "setup-footer"}}
<div class="enrol-footer" id="setup-footer">
  {{if .AllAddressed}}
    <a href="/" class="enrol-continue-btn">Continue to Dashboard &rarr;</a>
  {{else}}
    <form method="post" action="/setup/complete">
      <button type="submit" class="enrol-continue-btn">Skip remaining and continue &rarr;</button>
    </form>
  {{end}}
</div>
{{end}}
